# Frontend env — intentionally EMPTY for LAN / multi-user (remote) access. (PH-324)
#
# VITE_WS_URL and VITE_API_URL are deliberately NOT set here so the app uses
# HOST-RELATIVE URLs derived from window.location.host:
#   - HTTP: frontend/src/api/client.ts already uses BASE="/api" (host-relative).
#   - WS:   frontend/src/hooks/useWebSocket.ts falls back to
#           `${wsProtocol}//${window.location.host}` when VITE_WS_URL is unset.
#
# Hard-coding localhost here breaks every remote/LAN client (the browser would
# open a WS to ITS OWN localhost). Leave empty. Vite proxies /api, /mcp and /ws
# to the backend (see vite.config.ts). See .env.example for production (wss://) notes.
